+L115: The default `x-ms-version` being used by the Azure Storage data plane SDKs can be found in the changelogs in the following table:
+L116:  | cite6†Blob Service | cite7†ADLS Gen 2 | cite8†Files Service | cite9†Queue Service L117: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---
+L118: .NET  | cite10†Azure.Storage.Blobs†github.com | cite11†Azure.Storage.Files.DataLake†github.com | cite12†Azure.Storage.Files.Shares†github.com | cite13†Azure.Storage.Queues†github.com L119: Java  | cite14†azure-storage-blob†github.com | cite15†azure-storage-file-datalake†github.com | cite16†azure-storage-file-share†github.com | cite17†azure-storage-queue†github.com L120: Python  | cite18†azure-storage-blob†github.com | cite19†azure-storage-file-datalake†github.com | cite20†azure-storage-file-share†github.com | cite21†azure-storage-queue†github.com L121: JavaScript  | cite22†storage-blob†github.com | cite23†storage-file-datalake†github.com | cite24†storage-file-share†github.com | cite25†storage-queue†github.com L122: C++  | cite26†azure-storage-blobs†github.com | cite27†azure-storage-files-datalake†github.com | cite28†azure-storage-files-shares†github.com | cite29†azure-storage-queues†github.com L123: GoLang  | cite30†azblob†github.com | cite31†azdatalake†github.com | cite32†azfile†github.com | cite33†azqueue†github.com L124: The data plane Storage SDKs don't perform GA releases to the other official package feeds until the default `x-ms-version` for the release in question has full rollout in all regions. Therefore, the latest GA SDK release from the official package managers can safely be used in any region.
+L125: 
+L126: For a list of all other supported versions, and for information about using each version, see cite34†Previous Azure Storage service versions .
+L127: 
+L128: The 2026-10-06 service version includes the following features:
+L129:   * Added support for paginated to cite35†File List Ranges via the new `marker` and `maxresults` query parameters.
+L130:   * The `x-ms-content-crc64` response header will now be returned if the `x-ms-source-content-md5` request header is specificed for the following APIs:
+L131:     * cite36†Append Blob from URL L132:     * cite37†Append Blob L133:     * cite38†Put Block from URL L134:     * cite39†Put Block L135:     * cite40†Put Page from URL L136:     * cite41†Put Page L137: ## Specify service versions in requests
+L138: 
+L139: How you specify the version of the storage services to use for a request relates to how that request is authorized. The following sections describe authorization options and how the service version is specified for each.
+L140:   * Requests that use an OAuth 2.0 token from Microsoft Entra: To authorize a request with Microsoft Entra ID, pass the `x-ms-version` header on the request with a service version of 2017-11-09 or higher. For more information, see Call storage operations with OAuth tokens in cite42†Authorize with Microsoft Entra ID .
+L141:   * Requests that use Shared Key or Shared Key Lite: To authorize a request with Shared Key or Shared Key Lite, pass the `x-ms-version` header on the request. When using Azure Blob Storage, you can specify the default version for all requests by calling cite43†Set Blob Service Properties .
+L142:   * Requests that use a shared access signature (SAS): You can specify two versioning options on a shared access signature. The optional `api-version` header indicates which service version to use to execute the API operation. The required `SignedVersion (sv)` parameter specifies the service version to use to authorize the request made with the SAS. If the `api-version` header isn't specified, the value of the `SignedVersion (sv)` parameter also indicates the version to use to execute the API operation.
+L143:   * Requests that use anonymous access: When utilizing anonymous access against Blob Storage, no version is passed in. The heuristics for determining which version to use for the request are described in the next sections.
